# Secrets and settings for the Windows service.
#
# Copy is automatic: install-service.ps1 creates windows\service.env from this
# file on first install. Edit that copy, then apply it with:
#
#     .\windows\service-control.ps1 -Restart
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# The backend reads os.environ once at import and has no .env loader at all
# (backend/.env.example is documentation only). A service running as
# LocalSystem inherits nothing from the shell you installed it from, so this
# file is the only way secrets reach it -- install-service.ps1 bakes every
# KEY=VALUE line below into the service's environment block.
#
# Everything here is optional. Notification channels no-op and log when their
# variables are unset, so the dashboard runs fine with this file untouched.
#
# FORMAT: KEY=VALUE, one per line. # starts a comment. Quotes are stripped.
# Do NOT quote values containing spaces "just in case" -- they are passed
# through literally.
#
# SECURITY: windows\service.env is gitignored, and install-service.ps1 ACLs
# C:\ProgramData\SignalDashboard to SYSTEM + Administrators. It is still
# plaintext on disk and readable by any local administrator -- which is the
# same trust level as the service itself, but worth knowing.
#
# These are set for you by install-service.ps1 and must NOT be added here:
#   STOCKS_DB_PATH  STOCKS_LOG_DIR  STOCKS_STATIC_DIR
#   STOCKS_CORS_ORIGINS  STOCKS_OAUTH_REDIRECT_BASE
# Passing -PublicOrigin additionally derives these -- also do not set them here:
#   STOCKS_COOKIE_SECURE  STOCKS_HSTS_SECONDS  STOCKS_TRUSTED_PROXY_IPS
# STOCKS_REGISTRATION and STOCKS_INVITE_CODE are the exception: they belong
# here, and -PublicOrigin appends them with a generated code on first install.

# --- Core ---
# STOCKS_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# STOCKS_REFRESH_SECONDS=180

# --- Data sources ---
# SEC asks for a descriptive User-Agent with contact info for fair access.
# STOCKS_SEC_USER_AGENT=Signal Dashboard you@example.com
# Optional Alpha Vantage key (primary for technicals; Yahoo fallback if unset).
# STOCKS_ALPHA_VANTAGE_KEY=
# Optional Financial Modeling Prep key for official econ-calendar impact ratings.
# STOCKS_FMP_KEY=

# --- X (Twitter) watcher ---
# STOCKS_X_ACCOUNTS=realDonaldTrump,aistocksavvy
# Official API v2 bearer. Unset falls back to Nitter mirrors, which still store
# posts but flag the source as a warning until a real key is configured.
# STOCKS_X_BEARER=

# --- Email digest (SMTP; works with a Gmail app password) ---
# STOCKS_SMTP_HOST=
# STOCKS_SMTP_PORT=587
# STOCKS_SMTP_USER=
# STOCKS_SMTP_PASSWORD=
# STOCKS_SMTP_FROM=

# --- SMS alerts (Twilio) ---
# STOCKS_TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
# STOCKS_TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
# STOCKS_TWILIO_FROM_PHONE=

# --- Public access ---
# Who may create an account: open | invite | closed. Set to invite (with a code)
# whenever the dashboard is reachable from the internet -- being able to load
# the login page must not mean being able to create an account on it. Applies to
# BOTH the password form and OAuth sign-up; OAuth becomes link-only.
# install-service.ps1 -PublicOrigin appends these two with a generated code.
# STOCKS_REGISTRATION=open
# STOCKS_INVITE_CODE=
# NOTE: STOCKS_REGISTRATION=invite with an empty code is a boot failure, by
# design -- an empty code would compare equal to an empty submission.

# --- OAuth sign-in (optional; email + password + TOTP always works) ---
# Each provider is offered only when both its id and secret are set. The
# callback URL to register with the provider is:
#   http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/auth/oauth/<provider>/callback
# With -PublicOrigin, use the PUBLIC origin instead -- the provider compares the
# redirect URI byte-for-byte:
#   https://<machine>.<tailnet>.ts.net/api/auth/oauth/<provider>/callback
# STOCKS_OAUTH_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
# STOCKS_OAUTH_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
# STOCKS_OAUTH_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# STOCKS_OAUTH_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
